  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on the 6th October 2004 the proposed outbuilding at 297 Hanworth Road, Hounslow would be lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe outbuilding, being 6m deep and 7m wide, with a ridged roof with a maximum height of 3.8m, that would not take the total area of outbuilding and extension coverage to more than 50% of the dwellings curtilage, constitutes permitted development as defined by Schedule 2, Part 1, Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (as amended) and therefore does not require planning permission.\r\n"
